# ~/.mbsyncrc: sync the list with lab-mail into ~/mail/you@p7x.dev;
# see mbsync(1). Each host that reads the list installs its own copy,
# with its login in place of you@p7x.dev.
#
# This is for a login that may change the list, so the sync runs both
# ways and expunges on both sides: a move or deletion here takes effect
# on lab-mail at the next run. Fastmail still keeps every message. A
# read-only login syncs with Sync Pull and Expunge Near instead. Only
# the list's folders are synced, and the folders come from lab-mail.
#
# lab-mail listens only on loopback, so there is no TLS. The password
# is the one whose hash lab-mail keeps in imap-users. PassCmd reads it
# from a file of its own, readable only by you, so this config holds
# no secret. Pass <password> would put it here instead, and with
# neither, mbsync asks for it on each run.

IMAPAccount lab-mail
Host 127.0.0.1
Port 2143
TLSType None
AuthMechs LOGIN
User you@p7x.dev
PassCmd "cat ~/.config/lab-mail/password"

IMAPStore lab-mail
Account lab-mail

MaildirStore local
Path ~/mail/you@p7x.dev/
Inbox ~/mail/you@p7x.dev/INBOX

Channel lab-mail
Far :lab-mail:
Near :local:
Patterns INBOX Next Later Archive
Create Near
Sync All
Expunge Both
Remove None
CopyArrivalDate yes
